      "position_frame": null,
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "The paper (PMC5448097) explicitly names the junction as 'between Gln-131 and Gln-132' of \u03b21, but in the canonical UniProt sequence the only pair of adjacent glutamine residues in this region is Q130\u2013Q131 (canonical positions); position 132 is Val, not Gln. Python search confirms Q130 and Q131 are the sole adjacent Gln pair, indicating the paper's numbering is offset by +1 relative to canonical UniProt numbering. The corrected canonical junction is insert_after_residue=130 (between Q130 and Q131). Both flanking residues are confirmed Q by direct sequence lookup. The site lies deep within the extracellular domain (residues 37\u2013157), 94 residues from TM1 and 28 residues from TM2, well clear of both TM boundaries. Full-length membrane-anchored human KCNMB1 \u03b21-subunit with a Myc epitope tag inserted into the extracellular loop, co-expressed with FLAG-tagged BK \u03b1-subunit in HEK293 cells; the construct (myc c&e) was used to detect surface expression of the full-length protein by antibody labelling.",
